{232}{And so it was, above ground. There are many catacombs and tunnels lying beneath the surface. Some of the members attempted to retrieve it to use against Arronax, but they never returned. We were forced to battle him without it, and you know the consequences of that.}{And so it was, above ground. There are many catacombs and tunnels lying beneath the surface. Some of the members attempted to retrieve it to use against Arronax, but they never returned. We were forced to battle him without it, and you know the consequences of that.}{}{31}{}{ }
{233}{What does the device do?}{}{5}{}{242}{ }
{234}{I scared of this stuff. I go now.}{}{-4}{}{484}{ }
{240}{I don't like the sound of "catacombs and tunnels". Good day.}{}{5}{}{484}{re -5 }
{241}{Whut dat thing do?}{}{-4}{}{582}{ }
{242}{Extremely powerful mages have the ability to regenerate themselves whenever they are badly hurt, as I did. If one is powerful enough to hurt a master sorcerer gravely, the mage will retreat into his regenerative shell, and emerge stronger that ever. The device is the only way known to disrupt the regenerating shield.}{Extremely powerful mages have the ability to regenerate themselves whenever they are badly hurt, as I did. If one is powerful enough to hurt a master sorcerer gravely, the mage will retreat into his regenerative shell, and emerge stronger that ever. The device is the only way known to disrupt the regenerating shield.}{}{32}{}{ }
{243}{And disrupting the field kills the mage within?}{}{5}{}{252}{ }
{252}{Quite so. The technology of the device is designed to disrupt the field in such a way as to cause the shell to drain the life force, instead of regenerating it. Quite gruesome to contemplate, actually. Further, it is said that one who is killed in this manner is forever separated from this world, with no chance of being returned magically or otherwise.}{Quite so. The technology of the device is designed to disrupt the field in such a way as to cause the shell to drain the life force, instead of regenerating it. Quite gruesome to contemplate, actually. Further, it is said that one who is killed in this manner is forever separated from this world, with no chance of being returned magically or otherwise.}{}{33}{}{ru2118 }
{253}{How can I find this device?}{}{5}{}{262}{ }
{254}{Why don't you retrieve the device?}{}{5}{lf17 0}{272}{lf17 1 }
{262}{You must search the ruins of Vendigroth, in the wastes where the city once lay.}{You must search the ruins of Vendigroth, in the wastes where the city once lay.}{}{34}{}{ }
{263}{Why don't you retrieve the device?}{}{5}{lf17 0}{272}{lf17 1 }
{264}{Where can I find the ruins? The wastes are vast, as you know.}{}{5}{}{354}{ }
{265}{I have already retrieved the device.}{}{5}{gf2027 1}{464}{ss19 }
{266}{I had retrieved the device, but it was destroyed in my travels.}{}{5}{gf2028 1}{474}{ss19 }
{267}{I don't think I want to risk my life on fool's errands any longer.}{}{5}{}{484}{ }
{272}{I must conserve what little remains of my energy to banish you to the Void, once you have retreived the device. The banishment spell is rarely performed by a single mage, its power requirement is so great.}{I must conserve what little remains of my energy to banish you to the Void, once you have retreived the device. The banishment spell is rarely performed by a single mage, its power requirement is so great.}{}{35}{}{ }
{273}{Hold a moment - you are going to banish me?}{}{5}{}{282}{ }
{282}{Certainly. If we were to wait for Arronax to breach the wards, I fear the loss of life would be immeasurable.}{Certainly. If we were to wait for Arronax to breach the wards, I fear the loss of life would be immeasurable.}{}{36}{}{ }
{283}{It seems everything has fallen to me, once again.}{}{5}{ar20}{292}{ }
{284}{Where can I find the ruins?}{}{5}{ar-20}{354}{ }
{292}{The irony of all this is not lost on myself. One might almost believe the prophecies to be true. It does appear that you are instrumental in halting this cataclysm. If only this were not necessary. I had hoped that ... I had hoped if Arronax ever returned he would have realized the error of what he had done.}{The irony of all this is not lost on myself. One might almost believe the prophecies to be true. It does appear that you are instrumental in halting this cataclysm. If only this were not necessary. I had hoped that ... I had hoped if Arronax ever returned he would have realized the error of what he had done.}{}{37}{}{ }
{293}{Judging from my encounter with him, I'd say he had not.}{}{5}{}{302}{ }
{302}{Yes, yes. It is obvious to me that he has commited himself to a path which can only end in his destruction.}{Yes, yes. It is obvious to me that he has commited himself to a path which can only end in his destruction.}{}{38}{}{ }
{303}{What do I do once I've retrieved the device?}{}{5}{gf2027 0, gf2028 0, lf11 0}{312}{ }
{304}{If I must be banished, so be it.}{}{5}{lf11 1}{312}{ }
{312}{You must meet me at the site of the wards, the Ring of Brodgar, as they are now known. The barrier between the worlds is thin enough there for me to be able to send you across by myself. I would suggest you bring as much help as you can recruit, as it will be no easy task to defeat Arronax.}{You must meet me at the site of the wards, the Ring of Brodgar, as they are now known. The barrier between the worlds is thin enough there for me to be able to send you across by myself. I would suggest you bring as much help as you can recruit, as it will be no easy task to defeat Arronax.}{}{39}{}{lf6 1, ss 18 }
{313}{Off to the wastes, then.}{}{5}{}{0}{qu1051 2, gf2089 1 }
{314}{I'll do it, but can you clarify some things for me before I am off?}{}{5}{}{364}{qu1051 2, gf2089 1 }
{322}{[He sighs. It is almost as if you can see the weight of your words piercing his spirit.] I feel as if I have been waiting to hear those words since I awoke, those many years ago. I had hoped it would never come to this. From your tale I can only surmise that the Black Mountain Clan were banished to the Void to construct some sort of technological device to nullify the wards.}{[He sighs. It is almost as if you can see the weight of your words piercing his spirit.] I feel as if I have been waiting to hear those words since I awoke, those many years ago. I had hoped it would never come to this. From your tale I can only surmise that the Black Mountain Clan were banished to the Void to construct some sort of technological device to nullify the wards.}{}{40}{}{qu1016 4 }
{323}{So that's how Arronax plans to return?}{}{5}{na 799}{332}{ }
{324}{So that's how Arronax plans to return?}{}{5}{na -800}{499}{ }
{332}{[He cries out in anguish] Why Arronax? Why can't you see the folly of the path you've chosen? [He looks at you.] What are you going to do about this situation?}{[He cries out in anguish] Why Arronax? Why can't you see the folly of the path you've chosen? [He looks at you.] What are you going to do about this situation?}{}{41}{}{ }
{333}{What am I going to do? He's your son. What are you going to do?}{}{5}{}{202}{ }
{342}{When Mannox disappeared, I knew that something of that nature must have transpired.}{When Mannox disappeared, I knew that something of that nature must have transpired.}{}{42}{}{ }
{343}{And you did nothing about it?}{}{5}{}{347}{ }
{347}{I decided it was no longer my place to play a god. Who am I to decide who is right? When I took on that role before ... well, you have already heard what happened then.}{I decided it was no longer my place to play a god. Who am I to decide who is right? When I took on that role before ... well, you have already heard what happened then.}{}{43}{}{ }
{348}{You're going to need to do something, now. [Tell him your story.]}{}{5}{gf1099 1, gf2000 0, lf7 0, na 799}{192}{lf7 1 }
{349}{You're going to need to do something, now. [Tell him your story.]}{}{5}{gf2000 1, lf7 0, na 799}{192}{lf7 1 }
